# The thread sanitizer's known reports, for tests/run_all.py --tsan. Each
# entry is one known bug, still open, in the maintainer's known-bugs.md, or a
# race that is there by design. A bug's entries come out with the change
# that fixes it, and the sanitizer must then find nothing there. Anything not
# listed here fails CI.
#
# Entries name a function anywhere in either thread's stack, or a global
# variable; ^ and $ make the match exact.

# Known bug 20: the NV2A's registers are plain memory, which the game (through
# recomp_mmio_read and _write, and tests/nv2a_queue's DMA_GET poll) and the
# GPU thread read and write at once. Removed by the device register table
# (broader-fixes/CODEBASE.md R1).
race:^recomp_mmio_read$
race:^recomp_mmio_write$
race:^wait_get$

# Known bug 20, and by design: the push buffer, in guest memory, written by
# the game and read by the GPU thread's walk. On the console DMA_PUT orders
# the two, and here it is plain memory (above). D3D also patches the buffer
# just ahead of DMA_GET while the walk may be reading it, as on the console.
race:^nv2a_pb_scan$

# Known bug 20: the GPU thread's kick (s_kick_on, a switch cached lazily, and
# s_hurry), written by the game's thread and read by the GPU thread. Removed
# with the kick itself (CODEBASE.md R3) and the switch registry (R10).
race:^s_kick_on$
race:^s_hurry$

# Known bug 20: switches cached lazily by whichever thread reads them first:
# RECOMP_NV2A_QUEUE (nv2a_queue_on) and the software methods' mode
# (swm_mode). Removed by the switch registry (CODEBASE.md R10).
race:^nv2a_queue_on$
race:^swm_mode$

# Known bug 20: the GPU queue's counts, kept by the GPU thread and read for
# the log by the game's thread. No change planned yet.
race:^nv2a_queue_report$

# Known bugs 19 and 20: the display's and the GPU's interrupt registers are
# plain memory. The timer thread raises interrupts in them
# (kernel_pgraph_tick, kernel_vblank_tick), the GPU thread completes them
# (vblank_intr_tick), and the game acknowledges them (D3D's interrupt
# routine, through port/recomp_manual.c's sub_00194210), all at once, so one
# can be lost. Removed by the b1.3 hotfix's write-1-to-clear registers (its
# backlog row 11, broader-fixes/REVIEW.md change 5), which also takes out
# vblank_intr_tick and sub_00194210.
race:^vblank_intr_tick$
race:^kernel_pgraph_tick$
race:^sub_00194210$

# Known bug 21: CreateThread (src/platform/win32_compat.c) neither joins nor
# detaches the thread it starts, so each one's resources stay until the
# process ends.
thread:^CreateThread$

# By design: tests/fence_wait's fence word, in guest memory, written by the
# GPU side and polled by the game, as on the console.
race:^g_guest$
